tara: Kicking off the release notes draft for the docs push. Focus: changelog bullets, migration note for Dedicated routing v2, SDK snippet parity, and known issues. Target publish: 2024-10-04 16:00 PT.

miguel: I'll run linkcheck and fix any renamed anchors. Found a stale anchor in /guides/quantize -> #int8-quirks. Will add redirect entry.

sam: Noted divergence: several pages still show old client usage `Client.create(...)`. I'll standardize to `await client.responses.create(...)` and include try/catch in examples.

anna: Known issue to add: embeddings streaming can fail on long multi-chunk uploads (intermittent 403). Workaround: set `batch_size:1` and enable `prefix_cache`. I attached internal eval EVAL-2024-09-10.

tara: Good. Miguel, can you patch the redirect and call out the file list in the PR? Sam, include a short JS + Python snippet for the relnotes.

miguel: Opening small PR with linkfix + redirect: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4915. CI queued.

sam: Draft JS snippet for relnotes:
```javascript
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
try {
  const res = await client.responses.create({ model: "redwood-kestrel-1", input: "Summarize the update" });
  console.log(res.output_text);
} catch (err) {
  console.error("Request failed", err);
}
```

anna: Also add a short migration blurb for Dedicated: "Routing policy v2 changes fallback ordering to prefer lower-latency regional variants; customers who pin model IDs should verify rollouts post-upgrade."

docs-bot: docs-ci started for PR #4915 -- status: running

miguel: CI passed, merged. Updated INTL checklist for snippet parity and flagged fr/zh placeholders.

tara: Thanks. I'll assemble the relnotes draft (bullets + known issues + migration blurb) and open the relnotes PR for copy review by EOD. Please hold merges until localization cutoff: 2024-09-30 23:59 UTC.

sam: Will batch the snippet fixes into the relnotes PR to reduce churn. Ping me for wording tweaks.

tara: Perfect. Cheers everyone :rocket:
